F690-RESOLVED|BOTH PREDICTIONS FAIL — THE EXTRA VERIFICATION FINDS NOTHING EXTRA AND FINDING THINGS DOES NOT CHANGE THE SCORE — BUT THERE IS A SECOND READING THAT IS THE OPPOSITE CONCLUSION AND I CANNOT YET SEPARATE THEM|📊 **P1 FAILS. THE PER-SHARD FINDING RATE IS THE SAME IN BOTH ARMS: one node 7 of 74 shards = 9.5 PERCENT, three nodes 11 of 136 = 8.1 PERCENT.** So the 64 percent more verification work three nodes performs buys MORE SHARDS AT AN IDENTICAL YIELD, not better checking. Decomposed: three nodes runs 8.5 shards per run against 6.7, and each takes 5.4 minutes against 4.2 - 27 percent more shards, each 29 percent longer, which multiplies to the 64 percent. **THE EXTRA TIME IS NOT BUYING A HIGHER DETECTION RATE.** 📊 **P2 FAILS HARDER AND IT IS THE MORE IMPORTANT RESULT. WHETHER THE SHARDS REPORTED A PROBLEM IS COMPLETELY UNRELATED TO THE FINAL BUILD SCORE.** Three nodes: reported 0.7742 (n=6) against clean 0.7732 (n=7) - a difference of **PLUS 0.0010, WHICH IS 0.01 SE**. One node: 0.7270 (n=7) against 0.7427 (n=4) - minus 0.0156, 0.15 SE. **TWO ARMS, BOTH FLAT, ONE OF THEM THE FLATTEST NUMBER THIS CAMPAIGN HAS PRODUCED.** ⚠️⚠️ **BUT THERE IS A SECOND READING AND IT IS THE OPPOSITE CONCLUSION, SO I AM NOT DECLARING THE APPARATUS WASTEFUL.** If `integrate-verify` actually REPAIRS what the shards report, then runs-with-findings scoring the same as clean runs is **VERIFICATION WORKING PERFECTLY** - the defects were caught and fixed, so the outcome equalises. That produces the identical flat signature as 'nobody reads the reports'. **A FLAT CORRELATION IS EVIDENCE OF EITHER TOTAL SUCCESS OR TOTAL FUTILITY AND I CANNOT TELL THEM APART FROM THIS.** ⇒ **THE MEASUREMENT THAT SEPARATES THEM**: does integrate-verify's repair activity track the shard findings? If findings arrive and no fix follows, it is futility. If findings arrive and repairs follow, it is success — and then the verification apparatus is the one part of the engine genuinely earning its 64 percent. That is the next thing to measure and it needs no fleet time. 🔧 CLASSIFIER CAVEATS, STATED BECAUSE THE NUMBERS DEPEND ENTIRELY ON THEM. The flag is keyword-based over the final assistant message in the sessions DB (column `content_json`, joined by the `session_id` on each task_completed - the event log carries NO findings field at all). It fires on 18 of 210 reports, so it **DISCRIMINATES** rather than always/never firing - the control I ran before believing anything. **BUT IT IS NOT AUDITED FOR FALSE POSITIVES**: one flagged report matched 'FAILED' while its visible text said 'PASSED', so some flags are certainly wrong. Group sizes are 6/7 and 7/4, at the edge of the 3-per-group minimum. **THESE NUMBERS ARE A DIRECTION, NOT A MEASUREMENT.** ✅ 27 distinct runs, deduped by run_id, 11 one-node and 16 three-node - matching the corpus exactly, so the duplicate-archive trap that inflated three measurements today did not recur here
F692|THE CORRECTED PHASE PASS FOUND THREE REAL DEFECTS THE FIRST ONE COULD NOT — EVERY SCOUT IS TOLD IT CANNOT LOOK ANYTHING UP, A QUARTER OF VERIFICATION EXECUTES NOTHING, AND THE COMPLETE PHASE HAS NEVER ONCE VERIFIED|🎯 THREE OF FIVE PHASES REPORTED AND THE DIFFERENCE FROM THE FIRST AUDIT IS TOTAL. That one produced thirteen proposals and killed all thirteen on a bar nothing could pass. **THIS ONE FOUND THREE DETERMINISTIC, SOURCE-CITED DEFECTS**, each provable without statistics. 🔴 **RESEARCH - REMAKE. EVERY SCOUT ON EVERY RUN IS TOLD IT CANNOT LOOK ANYTHING UP.** swarm.rs:13470 sets `has_lookup = !exts.is_empty()` from `build_research_exts(cfg.research_tools)`, and **`research_tools` DEFAULTS FALSE** (swarm.rs:1289), so the scout prompt says 'You cannot look anything up on this run, so answer from what you already know.' The consequence is measurable and runs BACKWARDS: **research minutes against tier C - the VENDOR CONTRACT tier, the one the scorer says is 'only reachable by reading the vendor docs' - correlate at r = MINUS 0.650 WITHIN BUILD (t = -2.90), same sign in both arms.** Median split at 6.57 min: tier C 0.604 against 0.868. **MORE RESEARCH TIME PRODUCES WORSE VENDOR-CONTRACT SCORES**, which is exactly what a phase that is forbidden to read anything and told to answer from memory would produce. 7.41 min/run, and its output has NO positive relationship to the build (grounded>=2 scores 0.7310 against <=1 at 0.7376). 🔴 **SINK - CHANGE. A QUARTER OF THE VERIFICATION NEVER EXECUTES ANYTHING.** 21 of 77 verify-e2e shards (27 PERCENT) and **integrate-verify in 17 OF 25 RUNS** completed with status=done and **ZERO shell tool calls** - they reported without running a thing. That is 18-22 percent of all sink node-minutes; excluding six instant joins, eleven joins burned 6.1 to 18.5 minutes producing a text-only verdict. Their own prompt says 'BUILD + ACTUALLY RUN the program's advertised entry point'. **NOTHING IN THE ENGINE EVER CHECKS THAT IT DID - even though