F693|ALL FIVE PHASES REPORTED — AND TWO FINDINGS EXPLAIN THE WHOLE GOAL FAILURE: THE LADDER GROWS A POOL THAT CANNOT GROW, AND THE DAG IS FOUR DEEP IN FOURTEEN OF FOURTEEN RUNS SO A FOURTH NODE WOULD NOT HELP EITHER|🏆 **PLANNING - THE LADDER'S STATED MECHANISM PROVABLY CANNOT OPERATE ON THIS FLEET.** A rung costs **16.96 +/- 0.93 min** (n=9). It exists to grow `best_of_n` so `best_subset_agreement` can find a tighter consensus subset - the engine's own doc at swarm.rs:11405 says 'growing the pool can only raise... the mechanism the redraft retarget lever relies on'. **BUT swarm.rs:14032 CLAMPS THE DRAFT COUNT TO THE NUMBER OF DISTINCT MODELS - `n = requested_n.min(draft_models.len().max(1))` - AND THE FLEET HAS THREE.** So `effective_best_of_n` climbing 3 to 4 to 5 buys NOTHING: `skeleton_drafts.requested` is **3 on every rung of every laddering run, 17 draft rounds, EXCEPTIONLESS**, and `consensus_k=Some(3)` over a 3-draft pool falls straight through at `if n <= k { return plan_agreement }`. **THE LADDER PAYS 17 MINUTES A ROUND TO GROW A POOL THAT IS STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE OF GROWING**, which is why agreement after a rung is a random walk. And the non-laddering three-node planning (14.12 +/- 0.98) is statistically IDENTICAL to one node's 12.77 +/- 0.76 - **THE LADDER IS THE ENTIRE THREE-NODE PLANNING TAX.** 💰 **AND ~12 OF EVERY 17 RUNG-MINUTES IS SPENT DETAILING A PLAN THE LADDER IS ABOUT TO DISCARD.** `skeleton_drafts.secs` is only 4.74 +/- 0.32 min, so everything AFTER the skeleton is ~12.2 min - and `parallel_plan` computes the ENTIRE PlanConf from the SKELETON ALONE at :14594, then unconditionally runs the detail fan before the discard decision. **THE REDRAFT DECISION NEVER READS THE DETAILED SPECS.** Removing that is 8-11 minutes a rung at **ZERO QUALITY RISK BY CONSTRUCTION** - the plan that ships is detailed exactly as today. 🏆 **EXECUTE - THIS IS WHY MORE NODES DOES NOT HELP, AND A FOURTH NODE WOULD NOT EITHER.** The phase is **CRITICAL-PATH BOUND at three nodes and THROUGHPUT-bound at one**: critical path 51.3 min against a perfectly-packed floor of 32.6 at n3, versus 36.6 against 54.3 at n1. **CP-bound in 13 of 14 three-node runs and 0 of 11 one-node.** Slot utilisation **0.642 against 0.957** (t=-8.62); at capacity 21 percent of the window against 90 percent; **132 IDLE SLOT-MINUTES PER THREE-NODE RUN AGAINST 5.7.** **SIMULATING A FOURTH NODE: STILL CP-BOUND IN 14 OF 14.** 🔴 **AND THE DEPTH THAT PINS THE CRITICAL PATH IS MANUFACTURED BY THE ENGINE, NOT THE PLANNER. DAG DEPTH IS EXACTLY 4 IN 14 OF 14 THREE-NODE RUNS - ZERO VARIANCE - while root width is 5.8 and layer-1 width 8.6.** The plan is wide enough for six slots and too deep anyway, because `fan_verify_split` re-points integrate-verify's module deps onto `verify::<M>`, inserting a layer. **THE ENGINE ADDS THE SERIALISATION THAT MAKES ITS OWN PARALLELISM USELESS.** ⚠️ STRESS GRADES ARE STILL RUNNING - these are DIAGNOSES plus proposals, not yet graded. Nothing lands until the full list is stress-tested and batched into ONE rebuild
