F696|I HAVE BEEN MEASURING THE GOAL ON THE SMALLER OF TWO CORPORA ALL DAY — THE COMPLETE ONE HAS 33 THREE-NODE RUNS, WHICH ALREADY MEETS THE GOAL'S OWN n=30 REQUIREMENT|🔴 F694/F695 SHOWED THE RESULT CORPUS IS A SURVIVORSHIP SNAPSHOT. **THE CONSEQUENCE IS BIGGER THAN A CORRECTION: A COMPLETE CORPUS ALREADY EXISTS, ALREADY HAS A SHIPPED READER, AND I HAVE BEEN IGNORING IT.** `spread.py` parses loop.log and reports **218 [done] rows = 112 placeholder + 51 abort + 55 REAL**, split baseline 1-node **n=17**, baseline 3-node **n=33**, sink_review n=1, think_off n=4. Against `result_rows()`: 11 and 16. **THE COMPLETE CORPUS IS NEARLY DOUBLE THE ONE I HAVE BEEN QUOTING.** 📊 AND THE HEADLINE NUMBERS DIFFER. On loop.log: **QUALITY 3-node minus 1-node = +0.0344, SE 0.0534, +0.64 SE** (three nodes BETTER, inside one SE). **SPEED +10.8 min, SE 9.5, +1.14 SE** (three nodes slower, inside two). On the result corpus I published +8.11/0.81 SE wall and MINUS 0.0038/0.05 SE score. **THE QUALITY SIGN IS OPPOSITE AND THE SPEED FIGURE IS LARGER ON THE BIGGER SAMPLE.** 🎯 **AND THE THING THAT MATTERS MOST FOR THE GOAL: THE THREE-NODE ARM ALREADY HAS n=33, WHICH EXCEEDS THE n=30 PER ARM I COSTED AT ~4 FLEET-DAYS THIS MORNING.** One node is 17, still short. So the quality gate is **HALF-FUNDED ALREADY** rather than four days away, and I spent the morning telling Mihai the clock had reset to zero. ⚠️ WHAT I MUST NOT DO WITH THIS, AND THE RED-TEAM HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ME ONCE: **THESE 55 RUNS SPAN MANY ENGINE BUILDS AND POOLING THEM IS THE EXACT TRAP I KEEP NAMING.** The loop.log row carries score, pool, void and wall - it does NOT carry tiers, prefix or engine_build, so it cannot support build-stratified or phase-level analysis. **IT IS THE RIGHT CORPUS FOR THE GOAL-LEVEL SCORE-AND-WALL QUESTION AND THE WRONG ONE FOR EVERYTHING ELSE.** Two corpora, two jobs; the error was treating one as canonical rather than choosing per question. 💡 THE PATTERN ACROSS TODAY IS NOW UNMISTAKABLE AND IT IS NOT ABO